<bpmn:collaboration id="b_Collab_Proc_Element"><bpmn:participant id="b_Pool_Proc_Element" name="Prepare information element: element level (BPMN v0.6, refined design; runs once per required element)" processRef="Proc_Element"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N1"><bpmn:text>The AI may only propose. It cannot check, review, approve or release.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:association id="b_As_N1" sourceRef="b_T_Propose" targetRef="b_N1"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N2"><bpmn:text>The reviewer sees the readiness assessments with their reasons. Record-side refusals return here; a new review re-runs the checks on the current version.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:association id="b_As_N2" sourceRef="b_T_Review" targetRef="b_N2"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N3"><bpmn:text>A correction creates a new record version. Earlier checks, assessments, review and approval stay as history but are not effective for it.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:association id="b_As_N3" sourceRef="b_T_Correct" targetRef="b_N3"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N4"><bpmn:text>Approval preconditions: all checks passed on this exact version; evidence inspected; approver differs from reviewer and is in scope.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:association id="b_As_N4" sourceRef="b_T_Approve" targetRef="b_N4"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N5"><bpmn:text>A technical failure never sets Available = not met; it stays not yet assessed, with the reason recorded.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:association id="b_As_N5" sourceRef="b_E_UnresTech" targetRef="b_N5"/>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="b_N6"><bpmn:text>Dash-dot groups: refined design v0.6, not implemented in dpp-prep v0.3.2. Call activities: Figure 9c. Error boundary events: technical failure.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:group id="b_Gr1"/>
<bpmn:group id="b_Gr2"/>
<bpmn:group id="b_Gr3"/>
<bpmn:group id="b_Gr4"/>
<bpmn:group id="b_Gr5"/>
</bpmn:collaboration>
